      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "CRIMSON MISS (7) turned in a nice run last time to finish third over 1300m at Bendigo after being in the firing line on the corner. Enjoys a drop in grade so she is all set to build on that latest effort. QUEEN OF TUSCANY (1) was a nice winner two back then stepped up to BM66 grade last time and ran admirably. Much better suited back to this company. TESTING THE CUGAT (9) strode forward early from his wide draw when resuming last start over 1457m at this track then fought on gamely to finish third. That was an encouraging return and is trained here, so prospects look bright again. SMASH BLUE (4) didn't do a lot in the first four runs this prep but pulled one out of the box to score a narrow win last start. Should take confidence from that and draws to get the chance to go back-to-back. SAVETHEBESTTILLAST (8) hit the frame two starts ago at Tatura but ran below par last time when eighth and beaten 3.5 lengths over 1400m at Bendigo. Finds a nice race and can atone.",
